{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems\">2010 AMC 12A #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">2010 AMC 10A #16</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Trick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Trick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nondegenerate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has integer side lengths, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> is an angle bisector, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f142d92351c7c9e5a27f8a5c133742642df1c495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b997948ed19a3efcb8e9822baba6250aa5179b55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=8$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. What is the smallest possible value of the perimeter?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d72e028d2380c4544a6c8808e3e1375f668951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 33 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 35 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 36 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881a95e204e4affee6408670c1da184970c5e677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{BC} = \\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />. If we use the lowest possible integer values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> (the lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, respectively), then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/021137365a1c6ea35ebe3f63d73a2d05150e268f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BC = AD + DC = AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"237\" height=\"14\" />, contradicting the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality\" title=\"Triangle Inequality\">Triangle Inequality</a>. If we use the next lowest values (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/9596b5a2993d0f1ce48e542106bde5b216018861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830de927bd8077aa97abc0e3829961d12711fe7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />), the Triangle Inequality is satisfied. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf8a324ac91dc996a43ec591c840d26aae016a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 16 + 3 + 8 = \\boxed{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"23\" />, or choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Trick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Trick)\">Solution 2(Trick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Trick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5594ad66f9e2fe4a249db77ea195dec965dbed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{BC}=\\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a> so we let the lengths be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e3d817886b4d9dbd6bb74ad23463ed139ed68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88f825e8eca022f48ac1d2d41cd80ad6e5d9ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, respectively where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. Also since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e867467073fae9550c977a21ee2cb19426c4f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafb324902af9772751731e815ab84e05f4efcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, we notice that the perimeter of the triangle is the sum of these, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bca7bf0045f2bebdcec50116d14cd8b17253a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n+8n+3+8=11n+11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"222\" height=\"14\" /> This can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/96731e709e5aa63315ed904ef8db930d15dbc21b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and so the sum must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The only answer choice which is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d5a5da39b5452e6a8f6cf5da3edd2f1ce18ff3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} 33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" />. \n~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the Beauty of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rsURe5Xh-j0\">https://youtu.be/rsURe5Xh-j0</a>\n[he gives amazing (so beautiful ,so elegant ,just looking like a woww!!)  solutions]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A\" 